EF AI Workspace (#241): a picked skill survives a model switch, and the phone's «$» list sits above the message box.

- Model switch in a chat with no message yet (hooks/Input/useSelectMention.ts). Upstream's spec and endpoint
  switches start a fresh composer there (newConversation without keepComposerState): the draft token renews and every
  attachment goes, so a skill picked on the default «بصير لايت» (a context file, ADR-0022) or an attached file never
  reached «بصير بلس» or «بصير برو»; the typed text stayed. They now pass keepComposerState while the chat is unsent
  (no id, or «new»), which keeps the draft and its attachments, as upstream does when agent metadata re-renders the
  box. A chat with messages keeps its id and its files as before; moving from it to a new chat still starts clean.
  The speed selector, the model menu and the «بلا إنترنت ×» chip all switch through onSelectSpec; common/types.ts
  declares the option on ConvoGenerator, the type the hook receives newConversation as.
  - hooks/Input/useSelectMention.spec.tsx: the switch in an unsent chat, before any conversation, through the model
    menu's endpoint pick, in a chat with messages, and from a chat with messages to a new one.
- Phone skills list (Chat/Input/SkillsCommand.tsx): two and a half rows (140 px) under 768 px instead of four, so the
  list stays short above the box with the keyboard open; brand.css places it and slims its foot.
- The first-visit skills tip (Chat/Input/EfSkillsTip.tsx) sat between the box and the lists above it: opening the
  skills list now hides it for good (the employee has found skills), and it steps aside while «/» or «@» is open.
  - Chat/Input/__tests__/EfSkillsTip.spec.tsx: «فهمت», the skills list, and the «/» list.

